WEBVTT

01:04.147 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:07.233 --> 01:08.193
Careful.

01:09.444 --> 01:10.278
One, two.

01:11.196 --> 01:12.072
Be careful.

01:12.155 --> 01:14.365
Even if a million miles lie ahead of you…

01:16.618 --> 01:18.495
Please, mister!

01:18.578 --> 01:21.456
That's really upsetting me! Be gentle!

01:21.539 --> 01:25.460
…your greatest worry
is the one in front of you.

01:26.544 --> 01:28.630
-Can you lift this?
-One, two.

01:29.380 --> 01:32.050
Look, do we really have to take this up?

01:32.634 --> 01:34.969
Even if we do, there's nowhere to put it.

01:35.053 --> 01:37.597
You wanna sleep with this huge thing
in that tiny place?

01:38.807 --> 01:40.975
This is my wedding furniture.

01:41.476 --> 01:43.144
My very first.

01:43.228 --> 01:46.523
If you're downsizing,
you should take less stuff.

01:46.606 --> 01:50.360
Who cares about a mother-of-pearl wardrobe
these days? All wrapped up…

01:50.443 --> 01:51.986
It's Tongyeong mother-of-pearl.

01:52.987 --> 01:54.405
All right, let's take it up.

01:54.906 --> 01:56.324
-Let's take it up!
-Take it up.

01:56.407 --> 01:57.283
Okay!

01:57.367 --> 01:58.409
-One more person.
-Okay.

01:58.910 --> 01:59.744
Let's tilt it.

02:01.955 --> 02:02.789
Seriously!

02:04.082 --> 02:05.792
So why did we have to move?

02:05.875 --> 02:08.753
-Is that brat your only child?
-"Brat"?

02:08.837 --> 02:11.756
Cheol-yong's sister is a bus conductor.
She gives him pocket money.

02:11.840 --> 02:12.882
Is that brat…

02:14.008 --> 02:16.803
Is she the pillar of our home?
She's why it's falling apart.

02:16.886 --> 02:18.513
-Damn it.
-"Damn it"?

02:20.431 --> 02:22.016
Why are you always so tough on me?

02:22.809 --> 02:24.144
You'd better fix your hair.

02:24.727 --> 02:27.147
Do you go to school to make people laugh?

02:27.897 --> 02:31.025
-Pull it.
-Get ready to pull. Lift it!

02:31.776 --> 02:32.610
Here we go.

02:48.459 --> 02:49.711
What's wrong with this?

02:53.590 --> 02:54.591
Oh no.

02:59.345 --> 03:02.265
What's that?
Is it going to be a shoe cabinet now?

03:08.605 --> 03:09.856
Where are your aunties?

03:11.107 --> 03:14.569
They butted in at my circumcision,
so where are they now?

03:14.652 --> 03:17.238
They are busy because of the Olympics.

03:19.073 --> 03:22.493
I really don't get it.
Why are they involved in the Olympics?

03:23.286 --> 03:25.371
They say haenyeo represent Jeju.

03:25.455 --> 03:30.001
When they were given those roles,
they quickly made up with the government.

03:30.668 --> 03:32.795
What else is there for them to do
but make up?

03:35.757 --> 03:38.593
Where are you going?
You have a test coming up.

03:39.594 --> 03:44.349
You want me to waste money on college too?
Are you gonna move to a hut next?

03:45.350 --> 03:49.354
What about that darn wardrobe?
You said it was your wedding furniture!

03:50.230 --> 03:52.815
What? Am I starving you or something?

03:52.899 --> 03:55.026
Why do you always go on about money?

03:55.818 --> 03:57.070
Stop wasting electricity!

03:57.612 --> 03:58.863
Off to Cheol-yong's again?

04:47.787 --> 04:48.621
Come here.

05:03.136 --> 05:05.263
This is a little better.

05:05.888 --> 05:06.764
A little.

05:07.640 --> 05:10.935
I'll wallpaper the living room, too,
in one of those floral prints you love.

05:11.519 --> 05:13.104
It's already peeling.

05:15.148 --> 05:17.358
You picked the perfect spot
for the wardrobe.

05:17.442 --> 05:19.652
You can hang clothes
as soon as you come home,

05:19.736 --> 05:20.862
so the flow's perfect.

05:21.571 --> 05:24.282
You're the smart one,
so you pick everything perfectly.

05:25.033 --> 05:27.201
Why are you so talkative all of a sudden?

05:28.953 --> 05:30.496
Shall we go with floral curtains?

05:31.664 --> 05:33.624
Let's do it. Call the home decor store.

05:34.751 --> 05:36.586
-Call--
-It's fine.

05:39.172 --> 05:40.715
I like this place.

05:45.845 --> 05:48.222
It's just the wardrobe.

05:48.806 --> 05:51.059
It holds a special place in my heart.

05:51.642 --> 05:53.478
That's why I got annoyed.

05:57.065 --> 05:58.066
Now you're laughing?

05:59.359 --> 06:01.194
Have you ever lived in an apartment?

06:01.986 --> 06:04.197
How will you handle
being cramped up in here?

06:04.864 --> 06:07.617
Where will you hang blankets
or store big sauce jars?

06:08.201 --> 06:10.203
I've never been picky
about where we lived.

06:10.787 --> 06:14.332
Whether it was at your parents' house
or a one-bedroom rental,

06:15.208 --> 06:17.668
wherever you were was home to me.

06:20.797 --> 06:22.340
You should've married a rich man.

06:22.423 --> 06:25.426
Oh Ae-sun loves books
and enjoys being coy.

06:26.219 --> 06:28.554
You were born to be a rich man's wife.

06:30.014 --> 06:33.893
All the wives in Dodong-ri
are jealous of me.

06:33.976 --> 06:36.437
Who else gets to live
in a flower field like this?

06:38.606 --> 06:39.941
Really.

06:41.317 --> 06:44.487
This wallpaper is so outdated.
Where did you even get it?

06:45.279 --> 06:47.698
Even if a million miles lie ahead of you…

06:48.241 --> 06:49.909
Go. You'll get paste on you.

06:51.160 --> 06:52.912
…your greatest joy

06:53.871 --> 06:55.498
is the one in front of you.

06:56.958 --> 07:00.920
You gave your kid everything,
so now you're back to a street stall.

07:03.297 --> 07:06.259
You're just as stubborn as Gwang-rye.

07:06.342 --> 07:08.553
"Sun and the Three Aunties'" was fine.

07:08.636 --> 07:10.012
AUNTIES' SEAFOOD HOUSE

07:10.096 --> 07:13.224
I didn't even pay anything,
so why put my name on it?

07:13.307 --> 07:15.726
I don't like that. I really don't!

07:16.477 --> 07:19.480
After all these years,
does a sense of shame feed you?

07:19.564 --> 07:23.317
For so long, you've been clinging
to something that doesn't even make money.

07:24.986 --> 07:26.988
Charge me for setting up a stall here.

07:27.905 --> 07:29.365
Why wouldn't you charge me?

07:29.449 --> 07:32.702
I want to make it clear
I'm only selling appetizers.

07:32.785 --> 07:34.745
I will never sell what you sell!

07:37.999 --> 07:40.376
Why are you like this again? Why?

07:40.460 --> 07:42.962
How do you have time to play with a ball?

07:43.045 --> 07:43.880
Whatever!

07:43.963 --> 07:47.383
And that hair!
Where did you get the money to do that?

07:47.467 --> 07:48.301
Whatever!

07:48.384 --> 07:50.511
You're selling stuff again, aren't you?

07:52.763 --> 07:55.808
For heaven's sake,
you're driving me up the wall!

07:55.892 --> 07:58.269
-Whatever!
-She's soaking wet.

07:59.228 --> 08:00.938
Turn off the faucet. Hurry.

08:01.439 --> 08:02.940
Ae-sun's clock is smashed.

08:03.024 --> 08:04.984
You'll hurt yourself. Move your hand.

08:11.991 --> 08:13.910
He didn't even eat. Where did he go?

08:13.993 --> 08:17.079
Good grief, he's always going
to Cheol-yong's.

08:19.999 --> 08:23.377
Young children are so easy to treat, huh?

08:24.754 --> 08:28.049
No matter what you do, they still
look for you and call out, "Mom."

08:29.634 --> 08:32.094
Don't walk all over them
'cause they're easy to treat.

08:32.178 --> 08:36.098
A young leaf can be torn
by even a gentle rain.

08:41.395 --> 08:44.273
Auntie, when will I be fully grown?

08:45.942 --> 08:47.443
I'm not yet either.

08:47.985 --> 08:51.906
None of us have fully grown up…

08:51.989 --> 08:54.450
You even bought a big one. Why?

08:55.952 --> 08:58.913
Are you bribing us
to take good care of your wife?

08:59.413 --> 09:00.540
Yes.

09:00.623 --> 09:02.667
His people skills are improving.

09:06.003 --> 09:09.090
…but every time our hearts
felt growing pains,

09:09.840 --> 09:12.426
we all grew a little.

09:15.846 --> 09:16.722
What's going on?

09:16.806 --> 09:18.724
Hey, finish that later and come out here.

09:18.808 --> 09:20.017
Come out!

09:20.101 --> 09:21.435
Where do we stand?

09:21.519 --> 09:22.645
-Auntie!
-There you are.

09:22.728 --> 09:24.188
-To the middle.
-To the middle.

09:24.272 --> 09:25.189
Hey, come here.

09:25.898 --> 09:27.233
All right. Are we good?

09:27.316 --> 09:28.985
-Wait.
-What?

09:29.068 --> 09:30.778
-Come on.
-Leave my hair alone.

09:30.861 --> 09:33.531
One, two, say kimchi!

10:03.102 --> 10:06.314
Didn't I tell you to stop setting up
that stall on the street?

10:06.397 --> 10:10.318
I told you I hate
that you eat out on the street every day!

10:11.527 --> 10:13.070
What did she write here?

10:13.154 --> 10:15.364
COME AND CHECK US OUT!

10:15.448 --> 10:20.369
FRESH FISH DAILY, STRAIGHT FROM THE BOAT
MARKET PRICES ALL DAY

10:26.042 --> 10:28.461
There are moments when the heart grows.

10:29.837 --> 10:33.215
Seeing them on the street again
because of me, I made a vow to myself…

10:38.846 --> 10:44.894
never to take their dreams away again.

10:47.229 --> 10:51.067
SONG YEONG-SAM
SAN-108, BONGCHEON 5-DONG

10:55.529 --> 10:58.074
Boarding houses near the school
can be quite expensive.

10:59.533 --> 11:02.703
Though it's hilly here,
it's good for your health.

11:02.787 --> 11:04.830
INTEREST RATE SOARS
JAPAN'S ECONOMY UNSTABLE

11:04.914 --> 11:08.626
But if you could just fix the room door…

11:15.841 --> 11:18.844
He's just a kid. What's the big deal
if a kid comes and goes?

11:19.345 --> 11:23.641
Still, if you could just install
a latch inside…

11:25.768 --> 11:29.397
What, don't you trust us?
You're a funny one, aren't you?

11:30.231 --> 11:33.401
The one who lived here before you
never said a word.

11:33.484 --> 11:36.445
He called him over and looked after him,
saying how cute he was.

11:36.529 --> 11:38.114
Come on, take a look.

11:38.948 --> 11:40.616
Look how adorable he is.

11:41.617 --> 11:42.535
Right.

11:45.996 --> 11:47.248
He is cute.

11:48.290 --> 11:50.876
You know it's harder to find a room
or boarding house

11:50.960 --> 11:53.045
than an apartment these days.

11:54.255 --> 11:58.342
We have the luxury to choose our tenants,
but you don't have much choice.

11:59.468 --> 12:01.262
YEONG-SIM
YEONG-SIM'S DREAM

12:01.345 --> 12:04.932
Perhaps Yeong-sim had many dreams
because her family owned a home in Seoul.

12:05.015 --> 12:07.893
Let's all just be easygoing.

12:08.477 --> 12:11.772
Sure, easygoing.

12:12.356 --> 12:14.984
-It's me who needs to be easygoing.
-That reminds me.

12:15.818 --> 12:18.446
I'm saying this
because you remind me of my daughter.

12:18.529 --> 12:21.449
No boyfriends allowed.
If you bring one, I'll kick you out.

12:21.532 --> 12:23.159
No Park Chung-seop.

12:23.242 --> 12:25.411
If you were my daughter,
I'd break your legs.

12:25.494 --> 12:27.455
If I'm like your daughter, a door latch--

12:28.038 --> 12:33.419
DO NOT ENTER! KNOCK!

12:44.054 --> 12:46.307
Quiet. If they catch you, we're dead.

12:53.063 --> 12:53.981
Hello?

12:55.232 --> 12:56.275
Your son Cheol-yong

12:57.109 --> 12:57.943
is here.

12:58.861 --> 12:59.695
Yes.

13:01.155 --> 13:04.909
It's time for MacGyver to be on now,
but my son is still in his room.

13:05.951 --> 13:07.036
Yeah.

13:07.119 --> 13:08.162
Exactly.

13:09.830 --> 13:11.791
Cheol-yong really is something.

13:11.874 --> 13:16.462
If he was so afraid of his dad yelling,
he shouldn't have come last in his class.

13:17.087 --> 13:20.508
Not only did he come in last,
but now he's run away from home!

13:47.159 --> 13:48.118
Why lock the door?

13:49.245 --> 13:50.079
Privacy.

13:50.996 --> 13:52.498
What was that?

13:52.581 --> 13:54.834
Come on, get out of my room!

13:56.418 --> 13:58.587
This isn't your room.

13:58.671 --> 13:59.964
Did you buy this place?

14:00.047 --> 14:01.382
Whatever!

14:01.465 --> 14:05.261
Is that all you'll ever say to me?
"Whatever"?

14:06.637 --> 14:07.680
Get out!

14:07.763 --> 14:10.099
-You just don't get it.
-What did you say?

14:17.690 --> 14:20.067
Then what do we do?

14:22.236 --> 14:24.446
If you keep your mouth shut,
what should I do?

14:27.658 --> 14:29.451
So let's just call it quits now.

14:29.535 --> 14:31.161
You'd shave if you cared--

14:31.245 --> 14:32.663
It's not that I don't love you.

14:32.746 --> 14:35.082
Show me how I can stop loving you!

14:35.165 --> 14:36.876
So now what?

14:36.959 --> 14:39.169
Can you quit
and get your teaching certificate?

14:39.253 --> 14:40.546
I have my own level too.

14:40.629 --> 14:42.923
I have to marry
better than Suk-gyeong did.

14:43.007 --> 14:45.551
Are your worthless paintings
more important than I am?

14:45.634 --> 14:48.178
Should I stick egg cartons on the wall?

14:48.262 --> 14:51.265
Can you beat my father? At least shave!

14:51.348 --> 14:53.559
Do I mean less than your facial hair?

14:55.686 --> 14:57.563
Dad, give me the biggest one, okay?

14:57.646 --> 14:59.148
Give my sister the smallest one!

14:59.732 --> 15:00.566
Okay.

15:07.323 --> 15:09.033
The key is not there.

15:10.326 --> 15:11.577
Bu-seon, are you here?

15:12.286 --> 15:14.288
-Bu-seon!
-Bu-seon!

15:16.457 --> 15:17.458
Song Bu-seon!

15:25.090 --> 15:28.510
He's going through puberty!

15:28.594 --> 15:30.137
What's so special about it?

15:30.930 --> 15:34.350
Remember when you'd steal those croakers,
mackerels, and tilefish for me?

15:36.310 --> 15:39.521
Your mom said she wished she dropped dead.

15:42.816 --> 15:43.651
Here.

15:45.069 --> 15:45.903
Hey.

15:46.862 --> 15:48.072
I can beat my mom.

15:48.948 --> 15:49.949
I do beat her.

15:57.081 --> 15:57.915
Wait a minute.

15:59.500 --> 16:00.501
Why two forks?

16:02.753 --> 16:04.004
Why did Mom bring two?

16:08.801 --> 16:09.635
Bu-seon!

16:10.886 --> 16:11.720
Song Bu-seon!

16:12.930 --> 16:15.349
I think I chose the wrong place to live.

16:17.393 --> 16:19.269
-What are you doing?
-What are you doing?

16:19.353 --> 16:20.437
Song Bu-seon!

16:20.521 --> 16:21.397
Song Bu-seon!

16:22.022 --> 16:23.440
Song Bu-seon! Open the door!

16:23.524 --> 16:24.817
MILITARY MAIL
FROM PARK YEONG-BEOM

16:28.278 --> 16:29.113
Bu-seon.

16:30.823 --> 16:32.658
-Open the door!
-Open up!

16:33.158 --> 16:34.743
-Not gonna open it?
-What the hell?

16:34.827 --> 16:36.537
-Open this door now!
-Oh my God.

16:37.663 --> 16:38.789
Song Bu-seon!

16:38.872 --> 16:40.124
Who are you?

16:46.922 --> 16:47.756
Open it now!

16:50.134 --> 16:51.385
Are you crazy?

16:51.468 --> 16:53.637
What are you doing right now?

16:59.768 --> 17:01.854
Hey! Open the door now!

17:05.858 --> 17:08.944
Sir, ma'am, could you please
save me this one time?

17:09.028 --> 17:10.404
My dad will kill me for real.

17:11.030 --> 17:12.197
Please, just once.

17:13.615 --> 17:14.616
Just this once.

17:15.951 --> 17:17.494
The fluffy guy had the eyes

17:18.746 --> 17:21.498
of a mole being chased by a hunter.

17:27.963 --> 17:29.423
So I let it happen.

17:36.805 --> 17:37.681
Father, I…

17:39.641 --> 17:43.312
Well, I wanted to share some steamed buns.

17:44.188 --> 17:46.940
I was wondering how you were settling in.

17:47.649 --> 17:48.692
Well,

17:48.776 --> 17:50.944
why are you home so early?

17:51.695 --> 17:53.238
How about the factory?

17:53.322 --> 17:55.491
When were you ever interested
in my factory?

17:56.200 --> 17:58.911
This closet is more spacious
than it looks, isn't it?

17:58.994 --> 18:00.496
Dad, what about dinner--

18:01.705 --> 18:03.791
It's perfect for your blankets, isn't it?

18:03.874 --> 18:05.834
Yes, of course it isn't.

18:11.215 --> 18:12.424
"Of course it isn't"?

18:12.508 --> 18:14.718
Actually, you know,

18:14.802 --> 18:16.720
I really should go now.

18:16.804 --> 18:17.805
You know what?

18:19.139 --> 18:21.058
We provide the tenant with a wardrobe.

18:22.976 --> 18:24.436
She says she has to go.

18:24.520 --> 18:28.440
Wait… That's where my underwear…

18:29.149 --> 18:30.818
Why open a tenant's wardrobe?

18:35.155 --> 18:38.450
I think it's really time
for me to take my leave.

18:39.618 --> 18:41.203
Okay. Yeah, sure.

18:46.250 --> 18:48.210
But why are you standing there?

18:49.336 --> 18:52.047
Well, you know…

18:52.840 --> 18:56.301
I was just wondering if a new tenant came.

18:56.385 --> 18:58.428
You never cared
about what happens at home.

18:59.304 --> 19:01.640
You only care about
having the freedom to date.

19:03.100 --> 19:04.226
Come on. That's not…

19:06.395 --> 19:07.354
Come out.

19:08.647 --> 19:10.149
Come out now.

19:10.232 --> 19:11.775
-Dad, you know…
-Mr. Song.

19:11.859 --> 19:12.901
Landlord, my lord…

19:12.985 --> 19:15.404
Do you want to walk out?
Or should I drag you out?

19:15.487 --> 19:16.780
Come out!

19:18.115 --> 19:19.449
Cheol-yong, come out.

19:19.533 --> 19:22.494
Come on. We said we'd go easy on them.

19:22.578 --> 19:23.745
Park Cheol-yong!

19:25.497 --> 19:26.331
Come out!

19:26.415 --> 19:27.499
Park Chung-seop!

19:27.583 --> 19:29.126
Park Chung-seop!

19:35.340 --> 19:37.551
When Grandma Min-ok turned 60, she said,

19:39.469 --> 19:40.929
"Morally speaking,

19:41.430 --> 19:44.975
there is no place to hide in a house
but the wardrobe."

19:49.897 --> 19:50.731
Excuse me.

19:54.359 --> 19:55.194
Could you…

20:07.164 --> 20:08.207
I'm sorry.

20:09.958 --> 20:10.792
So sorry.

20:13.503 --> 20:18.342
It was embarrassing,
but that's how we first met.

20:21.970 --> 20:24.139
You punk. Cheol-yong, you little punk.

20:24.223 --> 20:27.017
Your father lost his nails.
Did you even know that?

20:27.100 --> 20:29.811
He works tirelessly
at the wholesale market.

20:29.895 --> 20:32.773
How dare you run away from home like…

20:33.482 --> 20:34.358
How can you…

20:40.364 --> 20:41.448
get smaller?

20:43.367 --> 20:44.284
He's smaller.

20:51.416 --> 20:52.584
Cheol-yong?

21:10.519 --> 21:11.353
Who are you?

21:17.109 --> 21:17.985
Are you

21:19.278 --> 21:20.404
a girl?

21:26.076 --> 21:27.035
Oh my God.

21:53.478 --> 21:54.855
So what happened

21:56.189 --> 21:57.274
to your hair?

21:58.066 --> 22:01.278
Did you cut it at home?
Is your family struggling?

22:02.195 --> 22:03.030
No.

22:04.364 --> 22:05.490
I was punished.

22:10.287 --> 22:11.788
You know,

22:13.415 --> 22:14.583
on the bag…

22:15.167 --> 22:18.503
By any chance,
does YEM happen to be "Yang Eun-myeong"?

22:19.338 --> 22:20.255
Yes.

22:20.339 --> 22:23.425
Why do you have Eun-myeong's initials
on your backpack?

22:23.508 --> 22:25.302
Are you guys close?

22:27.137 --> 22:28.055
Are you?

22:28.722 --> 22:29.639
We're dating.

22:32.726 --> 22:33.602
My goodness.

22:34.895 --> 22:37.147
-It's been 500 days.
-Where's the duster?

22:38.148 --> 22:39.816
You need to be beaten 500 times!

22:39.900 --> 22:42.152
But you two started dating
in elementary school.

22:42.235 --> 22:43.904
-We're much classier.
-Hey!

22:43.987 --> 22:45.072
Who told you that?

22:45.155 --> 22:45.989
Aunt Gyeong-ok!

22:46.782 --> 22:48.241
Call Yang Gyeong-ok over!

22:48.325 --> 22:49.451
Love isn't misconduct!

22:49.534 --> 22:51.036
What'd you say, you punk?

22:51.995 --> 22:53.538
This is a silent outcry

22:54.122 --> 22:56.208
A handkerchief of eternal nostalgia

22:56.750 --> 22:58.668
Waving toward the blue sea

22:59.169 --> 23:00.837
Oh, who could it be

23:01.546 --> 23:02.547
The first man to hang…

23:02.631 --> 23:05.884
At first, I didn't like her
because of her mustache.

23:06.510 --> 23:08.345
But after ten years of seeing her,

23:08.845 --> 23:11.181
one day, I stopped noticing it.

23:12.641 --> 23:13.975
What was I supposed to do?

23:14.893 --> 23:17.354
I don't want to hear this.

23:17.437 --> 23:19.564
I'm just a supplement here anyway!

23:20.315 --> 23:23.568
But this girl says I'm the best.
She likes me more than her brothers!

23:27.531 --> 23:31.159
Good for you, dummy. Happy?

23:31.243 --> 23:34.079
Yang Eun-myeong was just like Dad,
a sucker for love…

23:34.162 --> 23:35.705
The thing is,

23:36.289 --> 23:39.334
I've always liked naughty boys.

23:39.418 --> 23:41.086
…but not his taste in girls.

23:45.590 --> 23:47.175
But still,

23:47.259 --> 23:50.011
you shouldn't have run away from home.

23:50.637 --> 23:52.139
Do your parents know?

23:53.014 --> 23:54.433
They probably don't know yet.

23:56.393 --> 23:58.311
I left this morning.

23:58.395 --> 23:59.980
Which school do you go to?

24:00.981 --> 24:02.065
What's your name?

24:03.316 --> 24:04.609
Don't you have a name?

24:06.027 --> 24:07.112
Hmm… suk.

24:08.530 --> 24:11.324
Can't Suk speak?

24:16.246 --> 24:17.622
Bu Hyeon-suk.

24:22.419 --> 24:23.420
Hello.

24:27.424 --> 24:29.426
Why is your last name…

24:30.760 --> 24:31.595
Are you a Bu?

24:34.139 --> 24:34.973
Yes.

24:36.099 --> 24:36.933
I can't even.

24:37.559 --> 24:41.354
How can a love scandal
span two generations in such a small town?

24:41.438 --> 24:43.440
It happens because it's a small town.

24:43.523 --> 24:47.486
How did they have kids the same age
in such a small town?

24:47.569 --> 24:51.740
I couldn't come to help
with your move or to make kimchi.

24:53.158 --> 24:54.242
So, in other words,

24:54.910 --> 24:58.121
the two families had their meet-and-greet
when they were both pregnant.

24:58.788 --> 25:02.083
Hyeon-suk, never step on a pile of poop.

25:02.167 --> 25:05.629
You have to marry a man
like this lady's husband, okay?

25:07.422 --> 25:10.467
Hyeon-suk is also about to enter
Dodong Elementary, right?

25:10.550 --> 25:15.347
They went to the same school for ten years
in this small town, so no surprise there.

25:16.223 --> 25:19.684
Did you give your daughter your all
but go hands-off with your son?

25:19.768 --> 25:22.187
Do you know what kind of kids
your son hangs out with?

25:22.270 --> 25:26.233
Statistically, it'd be stranger
if they didn't get involved.

25:26.733 --> 25:29.027
There's this unbelievable girl
in the girls' class.

25:29.110 --> 25:32.197
He would never cause trouble with girls.

25:33.073 --> 25:35.784
Eun-myeong can't get along with them.

25:37.327 --> 25:39.746
He can't even hang out with his sister.

25:40.372 --> 25:43.208
Is it the same with sisters?
I can't hang out with mine either.

26:10.485 --> 26:13.572
But it's more to do with taste
than statistics.

26:13.655 --> 26:16.324
Actually, taste can run in the family too.

26:17.367 --> 26:21.997
Indecency runs in that family!

26:24.249 --> 26:25.417
I named my daughters

26:25.500 --> 26:28.503
Hyeon-suk for "virtuous"
and Jeong-suk for "pure."

26:28.587 --> 26:31.923
And I like those who are virtuous.

26:43.226 --> 26:45.353
Bu Hyeon-suk, get out of there now!

26:50.692 --> 26:52.235
At least come in and say hello.

26:52.319 --> 26:53.528
Are they getting married?

26:53.612 --> 26:54.863
In my opinion,

26:55.530 --> 26:58.533
Sang-gil had a bit of a crush on Ae-sun.

26:58.617 --> 26:59.451
Goddamn it.

26:59.534 --> 27:02.454
AUNTIES' SEAFOOD HOUSE

27:02.537 --> 27:03.788
He did have a crush.

27:07.000 --> 27:08.793
Passion runs in the family.

27:08.877 --> 27:11.921
Everyone in her family
knows nothing but romance.

27:12.422 --> 27:13.632
Are you having fun?

27:13.715 --> 27:15.800
Are you mad?

27:16.343 --> 27:18.345
Are you really that mad right now?

27:19.095 --> 27:21.056
What's the matter?

27:21.139 --> 27:23.600
You've had quite the spring yourself.

27:23.683 --> 27:24.934
There's no stopping spring.

27:25.018 --> 27:29.314
Could you have resisted the spring breeze?
Could you or couldn't you?

27:30.690 --> 27:33.860
My dear has a mouth but nothing to say.

27:35.195 --> 27:36.863
Kwon Gye-ok is having a blast.

27:36.946 --> 27:39.199
It's like she's waited for this
her whole life.

27:39.282 --> 27:43.244
If you're really careful, you'll lose
your son right under your nose too!

27:43.328 --> 27:46.206
Mother, it's your grandson
we're talking about.

27:48.917 --> 27:55.590
My strawberry-like innocence at 18

27:56.216 --> 28:02.430
If my own mom doesn't understand me
What should I do?

28:02.514 --> 28:04.182
Are you all planning to be singers?

28:04.849 --> 28:06.559
Stop watching that folk music show.

28:07.143 --> 28:10.230
President Roh Tae-woo
has declared war on crime and violence.

28:10.730 --> 28:12.941
People find ways to sleep together
while fleeing.

28:13.483 --> 28:17.237
Even in wartime,
flowers bloom, and people fall in love.

28:18.071 --> 28:19.072
Let them be

28:19.906 --> 28:21.700
so they can do their thing.

28:21.783 --> 28:24.911
To address urgent safety issues
like kidnapping and serial murders…

28:24.994 --> 28:27.831
They're now in the spring of their lives.

28:30.792 --> 28:32.585
GHOST
NOVEMBER 24, CANNES THEATER

28:37.173 --> 28:38.550
RACETRACK PART-TIME JOB

28:39.050 --> 28:41.970
SALES ASSISTANT WANTED

28:43.596 --> 28:46.433
EXCHANGE STUDENT IN TOKYO
LOOKING FOR JAPANESE TRANSLATION JOBS

28:46.516 --> 28:48.393
CLASS OF '87, ENGLISH LITERATURE
YANG GEUM-MYEONG

28:48.476 --> 28:52.313
Unlike TV dramas, studying abroad doesn't
throw you a golden lifeline in real life.

28:52.397 --> 28:54.232
KOREAN-JAPANESE TUTOR

28:55.275 --> 28:56.401
Darn it.

28:56.484 --> 28:58.903
Why did these kids post theirs
right next to mine?

28:59.487 --> 29:03.867
Life flowed at a step-by-step pace.

29:06.828 --> 29:09.914
You can put those posters up
whenever you want, right?

29:10.415 --> 29:13.626
Can you put them up anytime
as long as you meet your quota?

29:23.887 --> 29:25.054
Hello again.

29:30.351 --> 29:31.186
Are you

29:31.853 --> 29:33.855
looking for a part-time job?

29:35.023 --> 29:36.149
Yeah, I guess.

29:36.941 --> 29:38.318
But you know,

29:39.360 --> 29:40.361
this is my job.

29:42.280 --> 29:45.825
Anything that involves a brush is my job.

29:46.409 --> 29:48.453
Right, I see.

29:49.954 --> 29:50.955
Go ahead.

30:01.591 --> 30:06.846
GHOST
CANNES THEATER

30:14.521 --> 30:20.485
The premiere of Ghost is tonight
at 7:00 p.m. at the Cannes Theater.

30:23.321 --> 30:24.948
PART-TIME USHER
CANNES THEATER

30:29.285 --> 30:35.834
In Chapter Three, they begin
by mentioning the US, but as you all know…

30:35.917 --> 30:39.671
Come on, seriously.
Why is this woman fully clothed?

30:42.465 --> 30:44.259
Who told you to paint Ong-nyeo dressed?

30:44.342 --> 30:45.260
BYEON KANG-SOE 3

30:45.343 --> 30:46.803
That's what your Picasso said?

30:47.303 --> 30:50.473
People come to the theater
to see Ong-nyeo.

30:50.557 --> 30:53.852
They're not here to see
some greenery you painted.

30:53.935 --> 30:56.813
Go to the Piccadilly
or Danseongsa movie theater.

30:56.896 --> 30:59.399
Who paints Byeon Kang-soe
like a piece of scenery?

31:00.900 --> 31:04.112
Why do you keep trying to make art
with other people's money?

31:04.195 --> 31:05.780
Did you buy these paints?

31:05.864 --> 31:08.575
Did I give you this basement
as your personal gallery?

31:09.742 --> 31:12.245
I depicted the joys and sorrows
of Ong-nyeo and Kang-soe

31:12.328 --> 31:13.788
through these Korean mountains--

31:13.872 --> 31:16.541
What about my joys and sorrows?

31:16.624 --> 31:19.460
I'm the one
with the greatest sorrows here!

31:20.211 --> 31:22.547
A painting isn't a photograph--

31:22.630 --> 31:24.757
Oh, Artist Park!

31:24.841 --> 31:27.635
No, Artist My Lord! Your Artistic Majesty!

31:28.344 --> 31:29.762
Please spare me.

31:29.846 --> 31:32.807
I beg you, please. Please have mercy!

31:36.477 --> 31:38.396
-Here to see a movie?
-I'm not buying.

31:38.479 --> 31:39.480
She's here again.

31:40.064 --> 31:41.941
Lady! Stop scalping!

31:42.817 --> 31:44.861
Reselling our tickets is not allowed!

31:45.361 --> 31:46.863
A basement Picasso.

31:46.946 --> 31:49.532
There's a Picasso
in the basement of the Cannes Theater.

31:50.033 --> 31:52.994
He never talks back,
but he's as stubborn as a bull.

31:53.494 --> 31:55.955
He hangs his head
like he's done something wrong

31:56.039 --> 31:57.457
but keeps painting his own way.

31:57.540 --> 32:00.084
So who can blame the owner?
I'd lose it too.

32:00.919 --> 32:02.545
So he's actually an artist?

32:02.629 --> 32:04.213
I guess you could say that.

32:04.297 --> 32:07.008
Billboard painters
are usually no-name artists.

32:07.675 --> 32:08.968
But he doesn't get fired?

32:09.594 --> 32:10.678
The owner is a softy.

32:10.762 --> 32:11.763
Sorry?

32:11.846 --> 32:15.141
He feels bad for yelling,
so buys some snacks and slinks downstairs.

32:16.059 --> 32:16.935
I see.

32:24.067 --> 32:27.111
So how do you know each other?
Why did he introduce you to us?

32:27.612 --> 32:28.988
I just ran into him somewhere.

32:29.489 --> 32:30.865
Two tickets, please.

32:30.949 --> 32:33.618
But, honey, you run into them
and end up living with them.

32:42.919 --> 32:43.920
Next.

32:44.003 --> 32:45.463
TELL US THE NAME OF THE MOVIE

32:46.339 --> 32:47.340
Just one, please.

32:50.718 --> 32:51.594
Next.

32:52.512 --> 32:53.763
TICKET
GHOST

32:53.846 --> 32:55.598
-Excuse me.
-How many tickets?

32:55.682 --> 32:57.141
I don't want Ghost.

32:57.225 --> 32:59.519
Byeon Kang-soe is on later at night. Next.

32:59.602 --> 33:00.436
Did you see it?

33:00.520 --> 33:03.022
-Next!
-Do you want to see it with me later?

33:04.732 --> 33:06.234
Are you going to buy a ticket?

33:15.284 --> 33:16.995
I guess crazy guys watch movies too.

33:20.206 --> 33:21.082
Seriously?

33:44.814 --> 33:45.815
Ma'am!

33:49.235 --> 33:51.195
Ma'am, can you take over for a bit?

33:51.279 --> 33:52.530
Yeah.

33:57.618 --> 33:58.786
SHOWTIMES
GHOST

34:33.029 --> 34:36.324
It's Christmas, you know!

34:36.407 --> 34:37.241
So I'm here.

34:40.703 --> 34:42.288
Look at you in those overalls!

34:42.955 --> 34:44.082
You look thinner.

34:44.665 --> 34:45.708
You're still cute.

34:57.970 --> 35:01.182
Should I shoot them with the projector?
How do you know her?

35:02.266 --> 35:03.726
I don't know her.

35:03.810 --> 35:05.603
You still helped her get a job?

35:05.686 --> 35:06.521
Well,

35:07.230 --> 35:08.856
I can't say I know her,

35:08.940 --> 35:10.817
but I can't say I don't know her either.

35:11.317 --> 35:14.904
I see. A dangerous situation.
You two could become something one day.

35:14.987 --> 35:16.197
It's a safe situation.

35:17.115 --> 35:18.991
Nothing's safe between a man and a woman.

35:19.075 --> 35:21.285
Having a goalie
doesn't mean the goal's safe.

35:21.369 --> 35:23.913
You're both wearing safety helmets
just for show.

35:23.996 --> 35:28.376
But in your hearts, the sirens wail
and babies cry already.

35:28.459 --> 35:30.962
Why don't you just focus on
writing your script?

35:31.838 --> 35:34.132
Why is it safe? Are you siblings?

35:35.133 --> 35:35.967
It's just…

35:37.969 --> 35:40.805
We've run into each other
in some embarrassing situations.

35:45.351 --> 35:46.602
Why are they going there?

35:47.395 --> 35:48.729
Good times.

35:48.813 --> 35:49.689
Well, I guess…

35:51.440 --> 35:55.278
I'm not going to date anymore.
Especially not the box office girl.

35:56.320 --> 35:59.282
Hey, stop acting like you're all that
and just date more.

36:02.743 --> 36:04.453
This is still cold.

36:05.454 --> 36:08.207
It's a fleeting privilege in a short life.

36:16.299 --> 36:17.550
-You know what?
-What?

36:18.176 --> 36:19.969
-My family doesn't know.
-What?

36:20.595 --> 36:21.554
That I'm in Korea.

36:22.388 --> 36:24.432
The plan was to come
at the end of the month,

36:24.932 --> 36:26.350
so they don't know I'm here.

36:27.935 --> 36:29.478
You're such a bad boy.

36:30.062 --> 36:30.938
Should I tell them?

36:32.523 --> 36:33.357
Should I?

36:35.526 --> 36:36.777
Don't you dare.

36:36.861 --> 36:39.697
On the cuteness scale,
you're even cuter than puppies.

36:45.953 --> 36:47.622
DAEHAN NEWS

36:55.379 --> 36:56.214
Hey, man!

36:57.089 --> 36:58.633
Why are you leaving with that on?

36:59.592 --> 37:02.970
I chose this place
because of that thing up there.

37:03.596 --> 37:07.225
Up there, you'll see
the biggest Christmas tree in Korea.

37:07.308 --> 37:09.727
You won't see one that big even in the US.

37:11.520 --> 37:14.899
If I lived too close to the school,
my friends would be over all the time.

37:15.399 --> 37:17.735
Rooms near the school
are always in high demand,

37:17.818 --> 37:19.779
so the landlords are total dictators.

37:19.862 --> 37:22.740
And I love the fact
that meals aren't included here.

37:22.823 --> 37:24.325
I don't eat much anyway.

37:24.408 --> 37:25.952
HELP US FIND OUR MISSING STUDENTS

37:27.161 --> 37:27.995
Geum-myeong.

37:28.996 --> 37:29.830
Yeah?

37:30.414 --> 37:31.415
What is it?

37:33.042 --> 37:33.918
Not here.

37:34.543 --> 37:36.754
Look at this place. It's like Harlem.

37:38.756 --> 37:42.468
People who write stuff like that
on other people's walls

37:42.551 --> 37:44.053
are all sick in the head.

37:44.762 --> 37:46.722
Why would you pick such a dangerous area?

37:47.598 --> 37:49.850
I can't sleep
if you live in an area like this.

37:51.394 --> 37:54.063
Why are they fighting on my way home?

38:02.446 --> 38:03.864
That man's an artist.

38:05.491 --> 38:07.201
He is treasured by our theater.

38:07.994 --> 38:09.078
So stop overreacting.

38:09.161 --> 38:11.664
Who would be okay
with their girlfriend living here?

38:11.747 --> 38:13.165
I'd be crazy not to worry.

38:13.249 --> 38:14.959
What about this neighborhood?

38:15.042 --> 38:17.086
Everyone's doing just fine here.

38:19.088 --> 38:20.840
You should move. Let's go somewhere else.

38:22.341 --> 38:24.760
-What about my neighborhood--
-Where exactly?

38:24.844 --> 38:26.345
What, to your apartment?

38:26.429 --> 38:27.805
You don't really know Seoul--

38:27.888 --> 38:29.849
You're the one who doesn't know Seoul.

38:31.142 --> 38:32.059
You're the one.

38:35.855 --> 38:38.357
I'm saying this
because I'm worried about you.

38:40.151 --> 38:42.695
Just go home.
I'm not showing you where I live.

38:42.778 --> 38:45.990
All of Korea is like Harlem right now.
Serial murders and--

38:46.073 --> 38:47.366
Then go back to America.

38:47.450 --> 38:49.285
Go back, you Yank.

38:55.124 --> 38:56.459
Don't you dare follow me.

39:04.216 --> 39:06.761
I've never seen him smile. Ever.

39:07.511 --> 39:09.388
He keeps his mouth shut all the time.

39:09.472 --> 39:12.600
Even if I tried to strike up
a conversation with him…

39:12.683 --> 39:15.561
You could've just eaten the ones
that were open.

39:15.644 --> 39:19.273
Why do you think he bought the dumplings?

39:20.775 --> 39:23.235
So why did you yell at him again?

39:23.819 --> 39:25.446
You're wasting money on dumplings.

39:25.946 --> 39:27.323
Give them to him yourself.

39:28.157 --> 39:32.745
Our Picasso painted Madame Aema,
but he didn't use any skin-tone paint.

39:32.828 --> 39:34.538
How does that make any sense?

39:44.882 --> 39:48.969
AEMA WANTS TO RIDE AGAIN
MADAME AEMA

39:53.140 --> 39:55.810
How has he still not been fired
after this?

40:27.967 --> 40:29.677
Does he sleep here as well?

40:34.473 --> 40:37.309
BAEK SEOK'S POETRY COLLECTION

40:47.903 --> 40:50.614
ME, NATASHA, AND THE WHITE DONKEY

40:53.033 --> 40:55.369
THOUGH I'M POOR
I LOVED THE BEAUTIFUL NATASHA

40:55.453 --> 40:57.163
SO TONIGHT, THE SNOW WHUMPFS DOWN

40:58.956 --> 41:01.584
Because you're not interested in money?

41:01.667 --> 41:04.795
Because you're a noble artist, right?

41:06.464 --> 41:09.842
I'm not the one who's broke,
so why should I go on about money?

41:10.593 --> 41:12.595
You don't care about money,
so it's all fine?

41:12.678 --> 41:14.555
To be by your side,

41:14.638 --> 41:17.266
I have to think about money all day long.

41:17.349 --> 41:19.351
"How much were the pork cutlet
and tickets?"

41:19.435 --> 41:23.814
Even for a trip, I'd think,
"You have no money. It'd be a burden."

41:23.898 --> 41:27.193
We dated for three years
and never went to a nice restaurant.

41:27.276 --> 41:29.862
Just those stupid kalguksu and jjolmyeon,
over and over.

41:29.945 --> 41:32.907
Dating you makes me a cheap person!

41:32.990 --> 41:34.033
Is that art?

41:34.950 --> 41:37.036
Is that what your art stands for?

41:37.620 --> 41:42.458
How many more times will you come
and vent your anger before your wedding?

41:43.542 --> 41:45.503
Just leave. No need to save face.

41:45.586 --> 41:46.879
You can just go.

41:46.962 --> 41:48.130
You'll just let me go?

41:48.214 --> 41:49.215
-I'm tired too.
-What?

41:49.298 --> 41:51.759
You've been on six blind dates
since we got together.

41:52.551 --> 41:53.385
It's not fair.

41:54.553 --> 41:55.429
I'm done.

41:56.263 --> 41:58.390
I don't think I like you enough anymore

42:00.017 --> 42:01.602
to put up with all the unfairness.

42:04.647 --> 42:05.648
You have someone?

42:13.864 --> 42:15.032
You got a new girl?

42:16.116 --> 42:17.952
Is that why you're acting all tough?

42:18.661 --> 42:19.578
Like you are?

42:23.207 --> 42:24.583
Why aren't you answering?

42:25.626 --> 42:28.629
You have someone,
yet you're acting like the victim.

42:28.712 --> 42:31.840
So what do you want me to do?
If I tell you to stay, will you?

42:36.971 --> 42:38.556
Perhaps it was since then.

42:39.181 --> 42:43.310
My landlord's daughter
started kicking my shoes outside my room.

42:48.107 --> 42:49.108
Well,

42:49.984 --> 42:51.777
I brought you some dumplings.

42:53.112 --> 42:56.198
The projectionist insisted
I bring these to you.

42:57.366 --> 43:00.035
I'm really not sure
why I always run into you

43:00.119 --> 43:01.620
when you are

43:02.580 --> 43:04.540
in these embarrassing situations.

43:05.165 --> 43:06.417
I don't believe this.

43:09.753 --> 43:11.547
PART-TIME USHER
CANNES THEATER

43:11.630 --> 43:13.424
Did you help her get a job here?

43:15.426 --> 43:16.510
Well…

43:18.387 --> 43:20.806
You've been hiding a honeypot
in the theater?

43:21.557 --> 43:22.641
How nice of her.

43:22.725 --> 43:24.393
She even packed food for you.

43:24.476 --> 43:25.561
This is…

43:26.145 --> 43:27.146
Hey.

43:27.229 --> 43:29.982
Why won't you say anything?

43:30.065 --> 43:31.650
You should say something.

43:31.734 --> 43:33.110
I can't believe this.

43:33.902 --> 43:36.030
She'd fit right in with your family.

43:38.240 --> 43:41.035
Can't sort the wheat from the chaff?
You always come up empty.

43:41.827 --> 43:45.664
You dropped out of high school, right?
She goes to SNU.

43:46.790 --> 43:47.666
Watch your words.

43:50.127 --> 43:52.588
The fall breeze turned into
the spring breeze.

43:53.631 --> 43:57.009
The whistling sound
never ceased in my heart.

44:00.304 --> 44:02.973
THE WIND GOES WHOOSH
MY HEART GOES BOO-HOO.

46:48.722 --> 46:53.477
